published":"2026-11-15T07:48:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/playoffpredictions111426/cfp-predictions-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Lane Kiffin understands frustration as LSU's CFP hopes dashed with Texas loss","description":"Lane Kiffin said it was fair to question LSU's 6-4 record after Saturday's loss to Texas, a defeat that likely knocked the Tigers out of playoff contention.","published":"2026-11-15T15:44:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50488081/kiffin-understands-frustration-lsu-playoff-hopes-dashed","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Arch Manning leads game-winning drive as Texas stuns LSU","description":"Arch Manning found Raleek Brown for a 4-yard touchdown pass along the left sideline with 3 seconds left as Texas escaped Tiger Stadium with a victory over LSU","published":"2026-11-15T13:13:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50487515/arch-manning-leads-game-winning-drive-texas-stuns-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4832823/anthony-smith","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Smith_(defensive_end,_born_2004)"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Anthony Smith (defensive end, born 2004)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Smith_(defensive_end,_born_2004)","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:13Z","intro":"Anthony Smith (born May 28, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Minnesota Golden Gophers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Smith attended Shippensburg Area Senior High School in Shippensburg, Pennsylvania. As a senior, he had 64 tackles with 9.5 sacks and was named PennLive's Boys Athlete of the Year. He committed to play college football at the University of Minnesota."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Smith played in two games with one tackle and redshirted his first year at Minnesota in 2022. In 2023, he played in all 13 games and had 15 tackles and one sack. As a sophomore in 2024, he started three of 13 games, recording 27 tackles and tied for the team lead with six sacks. Smith returned to Minnesota for his redshirt junior season in 2025."}]}}